INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How many site visits are there and what are they?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 73, "section": "11.1 Periodic Monitoring", "score": 0.005099818, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 52, "section": "6.4 Unscheduled Visits", "score": 0.0021239663, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 9, "section": "Study Flowchart", "score": 0.0018895386, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "score": 0.0014269596, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 44, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "score": 0.0013831174, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "score": 0.0012303583, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 8263, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis\n\n\u201cSite visits\u201d could refer either to participant study visits or Monitor visits. For the main participant study flow, there are 9 numbered visits:\n\n1. Visit 1: Screening Visit.\n[Section 3.1.2 Overall Design \u00b7 p.26]\n\n2. Visit 2: Randomisation Visit (Baseline), beginning the 12-week double-blind treatment period.\n[Section 3.1.2 Overall Design \u00b7 p.26]\n\n3. Visits 3\u20137: five treatment-period visits, at Week 2 (Visit 3), Week 4 (Visit 4), Week 6 (Visit 5), Week 8 (Visit 6), and Week 10 (Visit 7).\n[Section 3.1.2 Overall Design \u00b7 p.26]\n\n4. Visit 8: End of Treatment (EoT) Visit, at completion of the 12-week double-blind treatment period (Week 12).\n[Section 3.1.2 Overall Design \u00b7 p.26]\n\n5. Visit 9: Safety Follow-up Visit, scheduled 35 days after the last dose of IMP (Day 105).\n[Section 3.1.2 Overall Design \u00b7 p.26]\n\nThe Time and Events Schedule also lists additional designations\u2014Visit 0 (Stabilization), Visit 1.1 (Baseline), V2.1\u2013V2.3, V7.1\u2013V7.3, and V8.1\u2014so I don't have this information to confidently state that the 9 main visits are the complete set of every operational visit in the schedule.\n[Section Table 1 Time and Events Schedule \u00b7 p.45]\n\nIf \u201csite visits\u201d means Monitor visits to the investigator site, no fixed number is specified; they are intended approximately every 6\u20138 weeks, with more frequent visits when new patients are included and frequency also dependent on site enrollment.\n[Section 11.1 Periodic Monitoring \u00b7 p.73]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "exactText": "- Visit 2: Randomisation Visit (Baseline), start of 12-week Double-blind Treatment Period\n- Visits 3-7: 5 visits during 12-week Double-blind Treatment Period\n- Visit 8: End of Treatment (EoT) Visit, completion of 12-week Double-blind Treatment Period\n- Visit 9: Safety Follow-up Visit, scheduled at 35 days after the last dose of IMP (Day 105).\nClinical assessments of disease activity will take place at Visit 1 (Screening Visit), Visit 2 (Randomisation Visit), Visit 3 (Week 2), Visit 4 (Week 4), Visit 5 (Week 6), Visit 6 (Week 8), Visit 7 (Week 10), and Visit 8 (Week 12).", "bboxes": [[89.99999999999989, 225.47998291015642, 541.6799999999998, 214.73497521784873]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "exactText": "Visits, Run-in = Visit 0 Stabilization. Visits, Screening Period = Visit 1 Screening. Visits, Screening Period = Visit 1.1 Baseline. Visits, Treatment Period = Visit 2 Baseline. Visits, Treatment Period = V2.1. Visits, Treatment Period = V2.2. Visits, Treatment Period = V2.3. Visits, Treatment Period = V 3. Visits, Treatment Period = V 4. Visits, Treatment Period = V 5. Visits, Treatment Period = V 6. Visits, Treatment Period = V 7. Visits, Treatment Period = V7.1. Visits, Treatment Period = V7.2. Visits, Treatment Period = V7.3. Visits, Treatment Period = V 8 (EoT Visit). Visits, Follow-up Period = V8.1. Visits, Follow-up Period = V 9 (Safety Follow-up Visit).", "bboxes": [[75.06486511230469, 495.4773864746094, 810.2346801757812, 247.2222900390625]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 73, "section": "11.1 Periodic Monitoring", "exactText": "For this trial, the frequency of the monitoring visits is intended to be approximately every 6-8 weeks. Frequent monitoring is expected when new patients have been included; thereafter there may be longer intervals between the visits. The frequency of monitoring is also dependent on the number of patients at each trial site.", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999983, 689.9039829101564, 552.5999999999999, 497.57497521784865]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": false, "condense_ms": 0.0010831281542778015, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 774.2761252447963, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 45, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 45, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.4477, 0.4013, 0.3611, 0.3555, 0.3474, 0.3335, 0.3312, 0.3255, 0.3172, 0.3139, 0.3134, 0.3093, 0.3091, 0.3068, 0.3035, 0.2979, 0.2898, 0.2891, 0.2878, 0.2859, 0.28, 0.2783, 0.2765, 0.2755, 0.2743, 0.2742, 0.2738, 0.2735, 0.2723, 0.2696, 0.2693, 0.2689, 0.2684, 0.2679, 0.2675, 0.2673, 0.2665, 0.2663, 0.2656, 0.265, 0.2641, 0.2637, 0.2625, 0.2615, 0.2615], "confidence_filter_dropped_scores": [], "confidence_filter_bm25_on