INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What assessments are performed at the Week 12 (End of Treatment) visit?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 9, "section": "Study Flowchart", "score": 0.9923638, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "score": 0.99187535, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 50, "section": "6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8)", "score": null, "scores": [0.9467938, 0.6296608], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 24, "section": "Primary Endpoints", "score": 0.75815266, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 7, "section": "Secondary Endpoints", "score": 0.41501737, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6234, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis\n\nAt the Week 12 End of Treatment (Visit 8) visit, the following assessments are performed:\n\n1. Endoscopy (sigmoidoscopy), with disease-activity assessment including endoscopy (colonoscopy or sigmoidoscopy) and collection of mucosal biopsies for assessment of mucosal healing, histology, and immunohistochemistry.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n2. Efficacy evaluation: 9-point partial Mayo Score without endoscopy and full Mayo Score.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n3. Blood sampling for PK assessments.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n4. Faeces sampling for calprotectin.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n5. Blood sampling for exploratory biomarkers; at Visit 8, the blood sampling must be taken when the patient is in a fasting state [ \u22658 hours].\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n6. Clinical laboratory test (blood and urine sampling).\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n7. Urine pregnancy test.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n8. Blood sampling for anti-TJ301 antibodies.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n9. Physical examination (body weight only).\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n10. Vital signs.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n11. 12-lead ECG.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n12. Diary review.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n13. Concomitant medications documented.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]\n\n14. Adverse events documented.\n[Section 6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8) \u00b7 p.50]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 50, "section": "6.2.4 12-week Treatment Period (Visits 3 to 8)", "exactText": "- Endoscopy (sigmoidoscopy) (Visit 8)\n- Efficacy evaluation (9-point partial Mayo Score without endoscopy at all visits, full Mayo Score at Visit 8)\n- Blood sampling for PK assessments (all visits)\n- Faeces sampling for calprotectin (Visits 4, 6, and 8)\n- Blood sampling for exploratory biomarkers (Visits 4, 6, and 8; At Visit 8, the blood sampling must be taken when the patient is in a fasting state [ \u22658 hours] )\n- Clinical laboratory test (blood and urine sampling; all visits)\n- Urine pregnancy test (Visit 8)\n- Blood sampling for anti-TJ301 antibodies (Visits 3, 4, 6, and 8)\n- Physical examination (Visits 4, 6, and 8; body weight only)\n- Vital signs (all visits)\n- 12-lead ECG (all visits)\n- Diary dispensing (Visits 3-7)\n- Diary review (all visits)\n- Concomitant medications documented (all visits)\n- Adverse events documented (all visits)", "bboxes": [[89.88, 432.47998291015625, 291.24, 421.73497521784856], [71.99999999999994, 453.98398291015627, 551.16, 443.69497521784854]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "exactText": "Clinical assessments of disease activity will take place at Visit 1 (Screening Visit), Visit 2 (Randomisation Visit), Visit 3 (Week 2), Visit 4 (Week 4), Visit 5 (Week 6), Visit 6 (Week 8), Visit 7 (Week 10), and Visit 8 (Week 12). During Screening and at Visit 8 (Week 12), assessments of disease activity will also include endoscopy (colonoscopy or sigmoidoscopy); mucosal biopsies for assessment of mucosal healing, histology, immunohistochemistry will be collected during endoscopy at these time points.", "bboxes": [[89.99999999999989, 225.47998291015642, 541.6799999999998, 214.73497521784873]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.0010416842997074127, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 672.9032089933753, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 44, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 44, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.5165, 0.6941, 0.6457, 0.6165, 0.5915, 0.5701, 0.5695, 0.5592, 0.5588, 0.5576, 0.5562, 0.5561, 0.5554, 0.5529, 0.5525, 0.5518, 0.5515, 0.5487, 0.5481, 0.5469, 0.5426, 0.5413, 0.538, 0.5301, 0.5296, 0.5295, 0.5288, 0.5278, 0.5263, 0.5234, 0.5228, 0.5228, 0.5223, 0.5223, 0.5201, 0.5198, 0.5183, 0.5159, 0.5148, 0.5144, 0.5121, 0.512, 0.5119, 0.5116], "confidence_filter_dropped_scores": [], "confidence_filter_bm25_only_scores_normalized": [], "hybrid_search": true, "cache_hit": true, "embedding_ms": 0.0, "db_search_ms": 566