INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What is the dose?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 23, "section": "1.2 Scientific Justification for Conducting the Trial", "score": 0.08882029, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 30, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "score": null, "scores": [0.083142914, 0.083142914], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 31, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "score": null, "scores": [0.059101548, 0.059101548, 0.053107902], "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6474, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis\n\nThe trial evaluates TJ301 doses of 75 mg, 300 mg, and 600 mg administered every other week. The 75 mg dose is anticipated to suppress the STAT-3 signal to baseline for at least one week; 300 mg and 600 mg every other week are anticipated to maintain trough levels >1 \u00b5g/mL and suppress IL-6/sIL-6R-mediated STAT-3 activation to baseline.\n[Section 3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial \u00b7 p.31]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 31, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "exactText": "The 75 mg dose every other week is, according to simulations, anticipated to suppress the second messenger signal to baseline level for a duration of at least one week and single dose data suggest approximately 80% occupancy after 14 days (Figure 3b). Both the 300 mg and 600 mg dose administered every other week are anticipated to suppress the activation of the IL-6/sIL-6R second messenger signal STAT-3 to baseline, as the trough levels are expected to be >1 \u00b5g/mL. The highest dose of 600 mg is selected to likely cover the highest anticipated dose in the therapeutic range of TJ301.", "bboxes": [[71.99